From: BoxDroid <boxdroid@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] nv2a/vulkan: invalidate only the downloaded surface range

Downstream status: not submitted upstream. The core renderer owns cache invalidation and GPU completion.

Retain transfer barriers and queue completion before host access.
Avoid cache maintenance over unused staging memory on non-coherent devices.

diff --git a/hw/xbox/nv2a/pgraph/vk/surface.c b/hw/xbox/nv2a/pgraph/vk/surface.c
--- a/hw/xbox/nv2a/pgraph/vk/surface.c
+++ b/hw/xbox/nv2a/pgraph/vk/surface.c
@@ -728,9 +728,13 @@
                           r->storage_buffers[BUFFER_STAGING_DST].allocation,
                           &mapped_memory_ptr));
 
-    vmaInvalidateAllocation(r->allocator,
-                            r->storage_buffers[BUFFER_STAGING_DST].allocation,
-                            0, VK_WHOLE_SIZE);
+    /* The queue completion and HOST_READ barrier above make this copy
+     * available to the CPU. Only invalidate the downloaded image, not the
+     * entire 64 MiB staging allocation. VMA aligns non-coherent ranges to
+     * nonCoherentAtomSize; depth/stencil packing fits within this host size. */
+    VK_CHECK(vmaInvalidateAllocation(
+        r->allocator, r->storage_buffers[BUFFER_STAGING_DST].allocation,
+        0, downloaded_image_size));
 #ifdef BOXDROID_XBOX_RUNTIME
     if (boxdroid_target_32a) {
         uint32_t sample_ordinal = __atomic_add_fetch(
